<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 1, ITEM 5 (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t1-design.md
        §3 Item 5). THE SIXTH MEMBER OF THE BROKER-LOOKUP FAMILY. lookupFilter, deleteConstraint
        and errorMessage are copied BYTE-FOR-BYTE from objects/Disposition__c/fields/Broker__c
        (itself copied from Broker_Assignment__c.Broker__c) - same referenceTo, same ACTIVE
        non-optional lookupFilter on Contact.RecordType.DeveloperName = 'Broker', same errorMessage
        text, same deleteConstraint. Do not vary the shape.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 WHY Contact.RecordType.DeveloperName AND NEVER Is_Broker__c.
        =====================================================================================
        MEASURED LIVE ON usman-dpeg, 2026-08-20 (see Disposition__c.Broker__c's own header for
        the full incident writeup):
            SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Contact WHERE Is_Broker__c = true                 -> 0
            SELECT COUNT(Id) FROM Contact WHERE RecordType.DeveloperName='Broker'   -> 19
        Is_Broker__c enforced the checkbox predicate for months on the other five siblings and
        silently refused every real broker in the org. It is retained on Contact but defines
        nothing. NEVER use it here.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 deleteConstraint IS SetNull, NEVER Restrict. DO NOT "FIX" THIS.
        =====================================================================================
        SetNull matches all five existing siblings (Broker_Assignment__c.Broker__c,
        Lease_Inquiry__c.Broker__c, Disposition__c.Broker__c, and both lookups on
        BOV_Broker_Change__c). Restrict would block legitimate Contact deletion for the whole org
        the moment any broker Contact had ever been picked on a listing. Disposition__c.Broker__c's
        own header states this DO NOT in terms and it applies identically here.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 THE SEED GUARD IS NOW INCOMPLETE - A DEV TASK, NOT RESOLVED BY THIS FILE.
        =====================================================================================
        scripts/seed-broker-contacts.apex mass-deletes broker Contacts with a STEP 2/3 guard that
        currently names only FOUR dependent lookups. With SetNull on all six lookups now that this
        field exists, re-running that script WILL NULL THIS FIELD with no error and no warning on
        every Broker_Listing__c that references a deleted broker. The guard's scan must be widened
        to cover Broker_Listing__c.Broker__c (and its header re-worded to name six lookups, not
        four) before this field goes live in any org the seed might touch again. Flagged in the
        implementing report for the developer agent - NOT actioned here (scripts/** is out of
        this agent's file ownership for this tranche).

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 WHAT THIS FIELD DOES NOT DO IN T1 - STATED SO NOBODY ASSUMES OTHERWISE.
        =====================================================================================
        Broker_Listing__c already carries Broker_Firm__c and Contact_Name__c as Text, and
        DispositionStageEntryService copies Disposition__c.Selected_Broker__c straight into
        Broker_Firm__c on auto-create. T1 adds NO stamp service for this new lookup, so:
          - the lookup is BLANK on every auto-created listing, and
          - the same lookup/text duality (and the same Contact-rename staleness documented on
            Disposition__c.Broker__c) now exists on a second object.
        That is acceptable for a schema-foundation tranche ONLY because it is written here. The
        stamp is a separate, un-scoped follow-up item.

        =====================================================================================
        ⚠ DO NOT WIDEN BrokerListingSelector.selectMostRecentByDispositionId IN T1.
        =====================================================================================
        That selector's field list is marked "THE FIELD LIST IS A CONTRACT", is WITH USER_MODE,
        and backs the Active Listing card. Adding this field to it is a separate FLS-risk change
        with a red-banner failure mode and is not part of this schema-only tranche.

        =====================================================================================
        RELATIONSHIP NAME: Broker_Listings.
        =====================================================================================
        Collision-checked against every field on Contact in this repo before choosing it:
        Broker_Assignments, Lease_Inquiries, Brokered_Opportunities, Brokered_Dispositions,
        Incoming_Broker_Changes, Outgoing_Broker_Changes are the occupants - none named
        Broker_Listings. The SAME string is already used as the relationshipName on
        Broker_Listing__c.Disposition__c (the Disposition side), but relationshipName is scoped
        per PARENT object, so that is not a collision - Contact.Broker_Listings and
        Disposition__c.Broker_Listings are two independent namespaces. Chosen as the bare plural
        because this field, like Broker_Assignment__c and Lease_Inquiry__c, is a role-named
        lookup on an object whose child rows exist largely to describe a broker relationship, per
        ARCHITECTURE.md §1's role-lookup naming exception. Settled BEFORE the first deploy, since
        a relationshipName is disruptive to change after.

        =====================================================================================
        ⚠ TEST FIXTURES.
        =====================================================================================
        Any Broker_Listing__c fixture that sets this field must use
        TestDataFactory.createBrokerContact(s) - the lookup filter is ACTIVE and non-optional, so
        a plain createContacts() Contact is refused at DML.

        FLS: applied in the consolidated permission-set pass, not this file.

        Risk: MEDIUM per the design doc - entirely because of the seed-guard gap above (dev task)
        and because a relationshipName is disruptive to change once deployed.
    -->
    <fullName>Broker__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The broker Contact for this listing. Selected_Broker text fields on this object are NOT stamped from this lookup in T1 - it is blank on every auto-created listing until a stamp service is built. See the XML comment in this file.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Pick the broker for this listing. Only Contacts on the Broker record type appear.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Broker</label>
    <lookupFilter>
        <active>true</active>
        <booleanFilter>1</booleanFilter>
        <errorMessage>Only Broker Contacts can be selected here.</errorMessage>
        <filterItems>
            <field>Contact.RecordType.DeveloperName</field>
            <operation>equals</operation>
            <value>Broker</value>
        </filterItems>
        <isOptional>false</isOptional>
    </lookupFilter>
    <referenceTo>Contact</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Broker Listings</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>Broker_Listings</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
